{"assumptions":["Procurement and receiving synchronize from a mock connected upstream source; no live upstream connector or file-upload flow is assumed.","Source record IDs are used to present repeated-synchronization update outcomes; duplicate prevention and persistence remain API-side behavior.","Calculation weights and feed quantities use pounds, costs use USD per pound, and a ton means a US short ton; entered units remain visible in the interface.","Wastage applies to estimates and projections only, without a separate wastage movement. Draft d1 references a conflicting ASM-3 wastage-based decrement assumption for saved feeding activities but leaves actual inventory decrement to API-side behavior; drafts d2 and d3 instead select actual-feed decrement without wastage. The web UI displays API-returned inventory outcomes and does not calculate the decrement rule.","Planned quantity is bunk rate in pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day multiplied by planned animal count; feed consumption and FCR use as-fed pounds.","Planned and delivered feed are allocated across lots in proportion to current animal counts in the pen.","Feeding activities are permitted without a matching plan; linked activities use planned quantity for variance, and plan mismatches are shown.","Authorized users can edit or cancel feeding activities and correct weight records; the interface displays accepted API outcomes.","Lot target weight and measured lot ADG drive projections when available; otherwise the yard expected daily gain is identified as the assumption, with any lot target override applied.","Feed cost of gain is reported separately; broader ROI uses available allocated purchase costs and sale proceeds and is labeled unavailable when required data is missing.","Date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters apply to the dedicated Feed-to-Gain report; lists support filtering and CSV export, with no custom report builder.","Sex is imported when supplied by the source; otherwise it remains unknown and the report filter offers known values only.","Lots and pens with current animal counts above zero are active.","Demo and presentation materials are provided in an in-app view.","The app is online-only."],"critic":[],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 22 requirements, about 2 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","passed":false},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths of 320, 768, 1024, 1280, and 1440 CSS pixels, all pages remain usable without horizontal page overflow; interactive touch targets at 320 pixels are at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.","text":"Every page shall use a responsive web layout for phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."}],"outOfScope":["Native iOS or Android applications, app-store release steps, and phone-only layouts; all product features are delivered in one responsive web app.","Durable storage and restart persistence for imported records, inventory, rations, plans, activities, measurements, and calculated values; this web spec verifies screens and values returned by the API.","Execution of procurement-source synchronization, source-ID deduplication and updates, failed-record processing, PO-line cost allocation, and persistence of PO-to-lot-to-pen relationships; the web requirements verify synchronization outcomes and mappings displayed to users.","Inventory movement accounting, wastage application to actual consumption, stock sufficiency enforcement, and atomic rollback of rejected activities; the web requirements verify returned inventory results and errors.","Calculation correctness for forecasts, ration optimization, inventory projections, feeding costs, lot rollups, weight metrics, FCR, profitability, and recommendations; the web requirements verify values and recommendations displayed from API responses.","Enforcing account authentication, role authorization, and server-side permission checks; the web requirements verify sign-in and role-specific screens.","Supplying or seeding demo records and producing report data; the web requirements verify supplied sample data and exported report files.","Live procurement or receiving connectivity, file-upload ingestion, self-service registration, SSO, and offline operation."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator-managed account exists and the sign-in page is open","id":"AC-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows email and password fields, no self-service registration or SSO controls, and the signed-in user's role and available pages","when":"The user inspects the sign-in controls and submits the account credentials"},{"given":"An Administrator is signed in","id":"AC-1.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows account controls with email, password, and Administrator and Operator role values, plus user, import, configuration, plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report controls","when":"The Administrator opens user management and the main navigation"},{"given":"An Operator is signed in","id":"AC-1.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report controls and does not show user-management, import, or configuration controls","when":"The Operator opens the main navigation and user-management page"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in for administrator-managed accounts without self-service registration or SSO, allow Administrators to manage accounts and assign Administrator or Operator roles, and display controls and pages defined for each assigned role.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","Q-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The mock source contains PO and receiving records with vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, and source fields","id":"AC-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The request targets the configured mock source and the screen shows the returned record fields and synchronization status for each record","when":"An Administrator starts synchronization"},{"given":"A source record has a previously imported source record ID and another source record has failed synchronization","id":"AC-2.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned update outcome for the previously imported ID and the failed record's ID and error, without showing the failed record as a successful import","when":"An Administrator starts another synchronization"}],"ears":"When an Administrator starts synchronization, the Feedlot web app shall request procurement and receiving records from the configured mock source and display returned records, source identifiers, per-record synchronization outcomes, and errors.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-20","ASM-21"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API provides a PO line mapped to multiple lots and pens, with available procurement and animal fields","id":"AC-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the PO line, source identifiers, related lots and pens, available vendor, cost, head-count, weight, breed, age, and source fields, and each pen's capacity and current animal count","when":"A user opens the imported record details or procurement traceability view"},{"given":"A PO line has a total cost of 1000 USD and two lots assigned 60 and 40 received animals","id":"AC-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows purchase-cost allocation values of 600 USD and 400 USD for the respective lots","when":"A user opens the PO line's lot allocations"},{"given":"The source response omits an animal's sex","id":"AC-3.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the sex field as Unknown","when":"A user opens that animal's imported details"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall display PO-line-to-lot-to-pen traceability, available procurement and animal fields, pen capacity and current animal counts, and lot purchase-cost allocations proportional to assigned received head counts.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","ASM-12","ASM-21"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API provides a lot target weight, receiving date, and measured ADG","id":"AC-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the target weight, lifecycle milestones, measured ADG as the projection assumption, and projected market date","when":"A user opens that lot's lifecycle view"},{"given":"The API provides no usable measured ADG and provides the yard expected daily gain and any lot-specific target override","id":"AC-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the projected market date, target weight used, and configured yard expected daily gain as the projection assumption","when":"A user opens that lot's lifecycle view"}],"ears":"When a user opens a lot lifecycle view, the Feedlot web app shall display target weight, lifecycle milestones, projected market date, and the growth assumption used, using measured ADG when available and otherwise the configured yard expected daily gain.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-8","ASM-9","ASM-22"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API provides an inventory item with stock values, entered units, cost, nutrition fields, and storage location","id":"AC-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the item name, category, available quantity, entered unit, cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values","when":"A user opens the feed inventory item"},{"given":"An inventory item is entered in tons with a cost per ton","id":"AC-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the entered units and normalized calculation values in pounds and USD per pound","when":"A user opens its cost details"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall allow users to view and enter feed inventory item fields, retain entered units for display, show normalized calculation values where applicable, and display opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","ASM-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Inventory, projected consumption, and a configured wastage ratio are available","id":"AC-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows estimates for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons and the wastage ratio used","when":"A user opens inventory projections"},{"given":"The inventory movement response contains receipts and feed consumption","id":"AC-6.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned stock movements and no separate wastage movement","when":"A user reviews the movement list and forecast"}],"ears":"When a user opens inventory projections, the Feedlot web app shall display estimates for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons using the configured wastage ratio in estimates and projections, without displaying a separate wastage stock movement.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-5","ASM-2","ASM-23"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user enters a ration name, type, ingredients, proportions, and intended animal type or weight range","id":"AC-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned ration's ingredients, proportions, dry-matter percentage, energy value, intended range, and calculated cost per pound in USD","when":"The user saves and opens the ration"},{"given":"A ration's ingredients have costs entered in different supported weight units","id":"AC-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the calculated cost in USD per pound and retains the entered units for display","when":"The user opens the ration cost details"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall allow users to create and view rations with ingredient proportions, nutritional values, intended animal or weight range, and calculated cost per pound using normalized calculation units while retaining entered units for display.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has entered nutrition or animal-range constraints and candidate mixes are returned","id":"AC-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each candidate's ingredient proportions, cost, and trade-offs without marking it saved or assigned","when":"The user requests and views candidate mixes"},{"given":"An optimization candidate is displayed","id":"AC-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned candidate as saved or assigned only after the action is accepted","when":"The user selects save or assign and that action is accepted"}],"ears":"When a user submits nutrition or animal-range constraints for ration optimization, the Feedlot web app shall display candidate ingredient mixes with costs and trade-offs and require an explicit save or assign action before a candidate is saved, assigned, or used.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen plan uses a bunk rate of 25 pounds per animal per day and a planned animal count of 40","id":"AC-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a planned feed quantity of 1000 pounds and the plan date, pen, ration, feeding time, cost, expected energy, and status","when":"A user generates the plan"},{"given":"A pen plan is for 1000 pounds and its current animals are split 60 to one lot and 40 to another","id":"AC-9.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows separate planned-feed allocations of 600 and 400 pounds for the respective lots","when":"A user opens the plan's lot allocations"}],"ears":"When a user generates a dated pen feeding plan, the Feedlot web app shall display planned quantity as the bunk rate in pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day multiplied by planned animal count, with plan details and separate lot allocations proportional to current lot animal counts in the pen.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","Q-6","Q-8","ASM-5","ASM-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Pen plans exist with delivery dates and statuses","id":"AC-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each plan's date, pen, ration, planned quantity, and Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped status","when":"A user opens feeding schedules"}],"ears":"When a user opens pen feeding schedules, the Feedlot web app shall show plans by delivery date and pen with planned quantity and Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped status.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A linked plan is for 900 pounds and an accepted activity records 950 pounds delivered","id":"AC-11.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows planned feed of 900 pounds, actual feed of 950 pounds, and a variance of 50 pounds, along with the activity fields","when":"The Operator opens the activity details"},{"given":"A pen contains animals from multiple lots and the API returns lot allocations for an activity","id":"AC-11.2","level":"ui","then":"The request contains separate lot allocations and the screen shows the returned delivered-feed allocations and corresponding lot consumption and cost rollups","when":"The Operator views the saved activity"},{"given":"No matching plan exists for the activity date and the save response is successful","id":"AC-11.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the activity as unplanned, the returned activity, and lot totals","when":"The Operator saves and views the feeding activity"},{"given":"An activity does not match the available plan date, pen, or lot","id":"AC-11.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a plan-mismatch indicator","when":"The activity is displayed in a list or detail view"}],"ears":"When an Operator records a feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall allow an activity with or without a matching plan, submit the activity details and lot allocations, and display the returned planned and actual quantities, variance when linked to a plan, inventory result, feed cost, energy, feeding status, lot allocations, and lot rollups.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","Q-7","Q-8","ASM-2","ASM-6","ASM-7","ASM-23","ASM-24"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API response for an accepted activity contains ingredient consumption and multiple lot allocations","id":"AC-12.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned ingredient quantities, as-fed lot quantities, feed costs, and separate lot allocations","when":"The activity and affected inventory or lot summaries are displayed"},{"given":"An accepted activity returns inventory results that include a wastage-based decrement","id":"AC-12.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned inventory result without replacing it with a web-calculated value","when":"The Operator views the saved activity and affected inventory"}],"ears":"When a feeding activity is accepted, the Feedlot web app shall display the inventory consumption and lot allocations returned by the API without asserting a web-side inventory decrement formula.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-6","Q-8","ASM-3","ASM-4","ASM-7","ASM-23"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Operator enters a feeding activity and the feed service refuses it for insufficient stock, returning unchanged totals","id":"AC-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen retains the entered values, shows the returned error, does not show the activity as saved, and continues to show the prior inventory and lot totals","when":"The Operator saves the activity"}],"ears":"When a feeding save is refused for insufficient stock, the Feedlot web app shall retain entered activity values and display the returned error without presenting the activity as saved or displaying updated inventory or lot totals.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API accepts an edit or cancellation and returns updated totals","id":"AC-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned corrected or canceled activity and recalculated inventory and lot total values","when":"The user views the activity and affected summaries"},{"given":"The API refuses an edit or cancellation","id":"AC-14.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned error message and existing activity details","when":"An authorized user views the action result"}],"ears":"When an authorized user edits or cancels a saved feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall display the returned activity state, inventory totals, and lot totals, or display the returned error if the API refuses the change.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-2","ASM-8","ASM-25"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Operator enters a measurement with date, number of animals weighed, average weight, total lot weight, gain since the prior measurement, and notes","id":"AC-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned measurement fields in the lot's dated weight history and trend","when":"The Operator saves and opens the lot's weight history"},{"given":"The API accepts a correction to a saved weight measurement and returns updated values","id":"AC-15.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the corrected record and returned recalculated metrics and weight trend","when":"An authorized user opens the lot history and metrics"}],"ears":"When an Operator records a lot weight measurement, the Feedlot web app shall submit the dated measurement fields and display the returned measurement in the lot's dated weight history and trend.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-25"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API supplies lot metrics for a lot with receiving date, entry and current average weights, feeding events, and target weight","id":"AC-16.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total as-fed feed consumed, FCR using as-fed pounds, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date","when":"A user opens the lot performance view"},{"given":"A feeding or weight event has been accepted and the API supplies refreshed lot metrics","id":"AC-16.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the refreshed metric values returned for that lot","when":"A user views the lot performance screen after the event"}],"ears":"When a user opens lot performance, the Feedlot web app shall display returned days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total as-fed feed consumed, FCR, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date, and refresh those values after an accepted feeding or weight event.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-7","ASM-2","ASM-22"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has purchase and feed costs but no sale proceeds or complete relevant costs","id":"AC-17.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows available purchase and feed cost components, feed cost of gain, and a broader ROI unavailable label","when":"A user opens lot profitability"},{"given":"The API supplies recorded sale proceeds, required costs, and recommendations based on feeding and weight trends","id":"AC-17.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows recorded sale revenue, returned broader profitability values, and returned feeding-adjustment or sale-timing recommendations","when":"A user opens lot financial performance and insights"}],"ears":"When a user opens lot financial performance and insights, the Feedlot web app shall display feed cost of gain separately, available purchase and feed costs and recorded sale revenue, label broader ROI unavailable when required data is missing, and display returned feeding or sale-timing recommendations.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-10","ASM-26"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API supplies dashboard data for lots, pens, inventory, rations, plans, activities, and weights","id":"AC-18.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows active lots and pens based on current animal counts above zero, animal counts per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily pen bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, total feed and cost, starting and current weights, weight gain, ADG, FCR, cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots","when":"A user opens the operations dashboard"}],"ears":"When a user opens the operations dashboard, the Feedlot web app shall display active lots and pens, operational counts and inventory, ration and plan information, feed and weight performance, energy use, and lot rankings.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-13"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API supplies aggregate values for active lots","id":"AC-19.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost","when":"A user opens the yard summary"}],"ears":"When a user opens the yard summary, the Feedlot web app shall display aggregate metrics across active lots, including total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-13"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The report has lot data including known and unknown sex values","id":"AC-20.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows matching lots with ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, and the sex filter offers known values only","when":"A user opens the report and applies date-range, breed, sex, or pen filters"},{"given":"A user selects report filters","id":"AC-20.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows only rows matching the selected date range, breed, known sex, and pen values","when":"The report results refresh"}],"ears":"When a user opens the dedicated Feed-to-Gain report, the Feedlot web app 